            "review_text": "Fredrik Ø\nLodz, Poland50 contributions\n0\nOkay\nSep 2017 • Friends\nVery nice place located in district 5. Visited on several occasions with two friends. \nWaterfalls, plants and a lot of fans makes it a fresh and comfortable place. They serve a mix of Chinese and Vietnamese food, both options really tasty and good. They serve and refill the ice tea free of charge. Actually they refill your glass so often that it's possible to get annoyed. Nevertheless, you won't leave thirsty. The prices are also somewhat above average, especially for drinks like coffee. 45 000 vdn for coffee with milk and ice is to much in my opinion, especially when you can get just as good coffee down the street for 15 000. Food prices are more sensible though, roughly 100 000vdn for noodle soup is not to bad quality and quantity considered. You also pay 3000 for a napkin and they charge a service fee of 5% in addition to the 10% tax fee. \nAll in all a okay place to have food everything considered.\nRead more\nWritten September 6, 2017",
