            "review_text": "David T\n87 contributions\n0\nWhere is The SaiGon One?\nAug 2014 • Family\nWe liked this restaurant so much that my brother and I visited this place 3 times in 2014. You can walked to this restaurant if you are in the backpacker area of PNL. The big Chinese red signs on glass door said it all. SaiGon 2 that means there is a SaiGon 1 but i have not find out where it is. This place served : breakfast (Dim Sum) Lunch and Dinner as well as Vegetarian and open from 6:30 AM until late 2:00AM\nWhen you walked in , on the left side you will see several fish tanks that contained live fish, lobster and frogs and turtles. The waitress will bring you to the table and depend how busy the place you may have to go up to the second floor. The place is air-conditioned and full of local and Chinese -Vietnamese's, that's a good sign.\nWe liked the Roast suckling pig dish, and the live fish and live crabs from the tank. The price is high compared to other dishes. But the taste is so fresh and sweat that you cannot resist. For the seafood we picked the fish right out of the tank: Ca Chem Steam with XO sauce, Crabs with bean thread noodles in a clay pot, Fresh Shrimp sauté with salted egg, and last but not least Chinese spinach sauté with garlic sauce. On our sub sequent visit we tried their famous: Ga Hap muoi hot (Steam chicken with rock salt in a clay pot), this is the dish you must try. The young chicken meat is tender and coated on the skin is a thin layer of remaining steam rock salted. No need for dipping sauce, just a squeeze of lime juice and a few stems of Rau Ram ( Vietnamese mints) , there you can have a very tasty morsel. I am guarantee this dish will give you a long last impression of the taste of Vietnam.\nThe price is high, the place is noisy, but the service and food is good. Must try....highly recommended.\nRead more\nValue\nService\nFood\nWritten July 2, 2015",
